/*  Books — `Pull a book on …`: `CheckPullStatement`, `ResolveModule` and the bundled books in
    `src/Interpreter/TypeChecker.Book.cs`, and the prelude `TypeChecker.WithPrelude` puts in front
    of every program.

    ★ A bundled book with a Cufet layer — `math`, `collections`, `chance` — binds AT that layer, an
    ordinary object defined in `src/Interpreter/Prelude/`, which this checker reads with its own
    parser. The rest bind as a `(BookType "name")`: `blueprints` with its one native member, and the
    language books with none.

    ⚠ The prelude's own bodies are not checked here. C# checks them in every program and accepts
    them in every program, so what they contribute is their declarations and nothing else.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// The prelude's object definitions — each bundled book's Cufet layer, and the rabbit — and its
    /// top-level functions, under the private names C# gives them (`match` in `regex.cufe` is
    /// `match in regex`), which is how a lowered pattern reaches its engine.
    Bind series of node to prelude-definitions, given (the text folder):
        Define found as a series of node.
        For each book in a series with ("blueprints", "chance", "collections", "math", "rabbit", "regex"), repeat:
            Try to:
                Define whole as read all from the file "{folder}/{book}.cufe".
                Define parsed as cast parser's program-tree on (whole).
                For each statement in parsed's children, repeat:
                    If statement's kind is "ObjectDefinition", insert statement into found.
                    If statement's kind is "BindStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)):
                        Define renamed as cast made on ("BindStatement", a series of node).
                        For each part in statement's children, repeat:
                            Cast renamed's add on (part).
                        Done.
                        The item 1 of renamed's children becomes cast quoted on ("{cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1))} in {book}").
                        Insert renamed into found.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            In case of failure:
                Define ignored as the message of the failure.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    /// Registers the prelude's definitions ahead of the program's, as C# does by putting them first.
    Bind void to register-prelude unto checker, given (the series of node definitions):
        For each definition in definitions, repeat:
            // A function is known by its signature; its body is the prelude's own business.
            If definition's kind is "BindStatement":
                Define function-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (definition, 1)).
                Cast one's bind-name on (function-name, a new binding {
                    the shape cast function-type-of on (definition),
                    the established-by cast named-reference on (function-name), the line 0, the permanent false,
                    the module false, the depth 0, the parameter false }).
                Skip.
            Done.
            Define name as cast def-name on (definition).
            Insert name into one's def-order.
            In one's defs, the entry for name becomes definition.
            In one's bundled, the entry for name becomes true.
        Done.
    Done.

    Bind node to book-type-named, given (the text name):
        Return cast made on ("BookType", a series with (cast quoted on (name))).
    Done.

    /// The types a bundled book introduces for the length of its pull — by name, as C# keys them.
    Bind series of text to introduced-types, given (the text book):
        Define lowered as book in lowercase.
        If lowered is "collections", return a series with ("matrix", "chase").
        If lowered is "blueprints", return a series with ("step", "pin").
        Return a series of text.
    Done.

    Bind node to introduced-type, given (the text name):
        If name is "matrix", return cast plain-type on ("MatrixType").
        If name is "chase", return cast plain-type on ("ChaseType").
        // `step` and `pin` are names for shapes of record — the fields sorted, as a record's are.
        Define text-type as cast plain-type on ("TextType").
        Define texts as cast wrapped on ("SeriesType", text-type).
        Define named as cast listed.
        If name is "step":
            Cast named's add on (cast record-slot on ("makes", texts)).
            Cast named's add on (cast record-slot on ("name", text-type)).
            Cast named's add on (cast record-slot on ("needs", texts)).
            Cast named's add on (cast record-slot on ("runs", texts)).
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Cast named's add on (cast record-slot on ("commit", text-type)).
            Cast named's add on (cast record-slot on ("name", text-type)).
            Cast named's add on (cast record-slot on ("source", text-type)).
        Done.
        Return cast made on ("RecordType", a series with (cast listed, named)).
    Done.

    Bind node to record-slot, given (the text name, the node shape):
        Define field as cast listed.
        Cast field's add on (cast quoted on (name)).
        Cast field's add on (shape).
        Return field.
    Done.

    /// `RegisterPulledBookTypes`: every type a book pulled anywhere in the program introduces, in
    /// scope for gathering signatures — giving back the names it added, so only those are taken away.
    Bind series of text to register-pulled-book-types unto checker, given (the node program):
        Define added as a series of text.
        Cast one's gather-pulled-types on (program, added).
        Return added.
    Done.

    Bind void to gather-pulled-types unto checker, given (the node tree, the series of text added):
        Define kind as tree's kind.
        If kind is "atom" or kind is "CufetAxiomDefinition", return.
        If kind is "PullStatement":
            For each pulled in (cast field-of on (tree, 1))'s children, repeat:
                Define book as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pulled, 1)).
                For each introduced in cast introduced-types on (book), repeat:
                    Define key as introduced in lowercase.
                    Define outermost-types as item 1 of one's type-scopes.
                    If (the entry for key in outermost-types) is void:
                        In outermost-types, the entry for key becomes cast introduced-type on (introduced).
                        Insert key into added.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Cast one's gather-pulled-types on (child, added).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The shape with every name a pulled book has put in scope replaced by that type.
    Bind node to scope-resolved unto checker, given (the node shape):
        If shape's kind is "atom", return shape.
        If shape's kind is "ObjectType":
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)).
            If (the entry for name in one's defs) is void:
                Define introduced as cast one's scoped-type on (name in lowercase).
                If cast is-none on (introduced) is false, return introduced.
            Done.
            Return shape.
        Done.
        Define rebuilt as a new node { the kind shape's kind, the word shape's word, the children a series of node }.
        For each inner in shape's children, repeat:
            Cast rebuilt's add on (cast one's scope-resolved on (inner)).
        Done.
        Return rebuilt.
    Done.

    /// After checking: every type written as the bare name of a type a pulled book introduces is
    /// replaced, where it stands, by that type — `series of step` becomes a series of the record —
    /// and every filled type by its filling's own name, `stack of number`. C# does the same so the
    /// compiler meets one spelling of one type.
    Bind void to resolve-book-shells unto checker, given (the node tree):
        If tree's kind is "atom" or tree's kind is "CufetAxiomDefinition", return.
        Define place as 0.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define resolved as cast unknown-type.
            If cast is-filled-type on (child):
                The resolved becomes cast made on ("ObjectType", a series with (cast quoted on (cast filled-type-name on (child)), cast listed)).
            Done.
            Otherwise if child's kind is "ObjectType" and the number of (cast field-of on (child, 2))'s children is 0:
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (child, 1)).
                If (the entry for name in one's defs) is void:
                    The resolved becomes cast one's scoped-type on (name in lowercase).
                Done.
            Done.
            If cast is-none on (resolved), cast one's resolve-book-shells on (child).
            Otherwise, cast rewrite-field on (tree, place, resolved).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The type a book's pull put in scope under this name, or none.
    Bind node to scoped-type unto checker, given (the text name):
        Define back as the number of one's type-scopes.
        While back is greater than 0, repeat:
            Define found as the entry for name in item back of one's type-scopes.
            If found is not void, return found.
            Decrement back by 1.
        Done.
        Return cast unknown-type.
    Done.

    Bind void to register-scoped-type unto checker, given (the text name, the node shape):
        Define innermost-types as item (the number of one's type-scopes) of one's type-scopes.
        In innermost-types, the entry for name becomes shape.
    Done.

    Bind fact to has-scoped-type unto checker, given (the text name):
        For each types in one's type-scopes, repeat:
            If (the entry for name in types) is not void, return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// What `Pull … <name>` reaches — `ResolveModule` — or the refusal.
    Bind node or failure to resolve-module unto checker, given (the text name, the fact via-book-form,
            the number at-row):
        Define lowered as name in lowercase.
        If lowered is "rabbit":
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("a rabbit isn't a book",
                "Pulling a rabbit opens its region, which the 'book on' spelling does not do",
                at-row, "pull a rabbit as though it were a book",
                "Write 'Pull a rabbit.' — or 'Pull a rabbit as <name>.' to give it a name.")).
        Done.
        If cast is-a-book on (name):
            If via-book-form is false:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is a book, so it is pulled as one",
                    "The plain form is for a module you have one of; a book owns no lifetime, so it is consulted rather than held",
                    at-row, "pull '{name}' with the plain form",
                    "Write 'Pull a book on {name}.' — or 'Pull books on {name}, and <other>.' for several at once.")).
            Done.
            // A book with a Cufet layer binds at the layer; the rest are a native book.
            If (the entry for lowered in one's defs) is not void, return cast object-type-named on (lowered).
            Return cast book-type-named on (lowered).
        Done.
        Define written as the entry for name in one's defs.
        If written is not void:
            If cast is-module-definition on (written) is false:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is not a module, so it can't be pulled",
                    "Pulling brings a module into scope, and '{name}' doesn't say it is one",
                    at-row, "pull '{name}'",
                    "Add 'and module' to its definition: 'Define object {name} with (...) and module:'.")).
            Done.
            Define is-book as cast conforms-as on (written, "book").
            If is-book and via-book-form is false:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is a book, so it is pulled as one",
                    "'{name}' says 'and book', so it owns no lifetime of its own — which is why it is consulted rather than held",
                    at-row, "pull '{name}' as though you had one of it", "Write 'Pull a book on {name}.' instead.")).
            Done.
            If is-book is false and via-book-form:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is not a book",
                    "'{name}' is a module: it may own a lifetime of its own, so you have one of it rather than consulting it",
                    at-row, "pull '{name}' as a book",
                    "Write 'Pull a {name}.' instead — or add 'and book' to its definition if it owns no lifetime.")).
            Done.
            Return cast object-type-named on (name).
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("there is nothing named '{name}' to pull", "",
            at-row, "pull '{name}'",
            "Pull one of the bundled books ('blueprints', 'c-language', 'chance', 'collections', 'cufet', 'math', 'regex'), or define an object named '{name}' as a module: 'Define object {name} with (...) and module:'.")).
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-pull unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        Define carried-reach as cast one's carried-beyond-reach on (statement).
        If carried-reach is not "", return a failure (cast not-judged on (carried-reach)).
        Define via-book-form as cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)).
        Cast one's enter-scope.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children, repeat:
            Define book as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)).
            Define local as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 2)).
            Define bound as cast one's resolve-module on (book, via-book-form, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's bind-name on (local, a new binding {
                the shape bound, the established-by cast placed-reference on (local, at-row, cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 4))),
                the line at-row, the permanent false, the module true, the depth 0, the parameter false }).
            If cast is-a-book on (book):
                For each introduced in cast introduced-types on (book), repeat:
                    Cast one's register-scoped-type on (introduced, cast introduced-type on (introduced)).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        // Its modules' needs are verified here, with what is visible here, once checking is done.
        Define visible as a series of text.
        For each scope in one's scopes, repeat:
            For each pair in scope, repeat:
                Insert the key of pair into visible.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define opens-region as false.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children, repeat:
            Define book as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)).
            Insert a new pending-pull { the module book, the line at-row, the visible visible } into one's pending-pulls.
            Define written as the entry for book in one's defs.
            If written is not void:
                If cast conforms-as on (written, "region") and (the entry for book in one's bundled) is void:
                    The opens-region becomes true.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        If opens-region, increment one's rabbit-depth by 1.
        Cast one's check-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        If opens-region, decrement one's rabbit-depth by 1.
        Cast one's exit-scope.
    Done.

    /// Each module pulled has what its bodies reached for, where it was pulled.
    Bind void or failure to check-pending-pulls unto checker:
        For each pending in one's pending-pulls, repeat:
            Define needs as the entry for pending's module in one's module-needs.
            If needs is not void:
                Define seen as a map from text to fact.
                For each name in pending's visible, repeat:
                    In seen, the entry for name becomes true.
                Done.
                Define missing-set as a map from text to fact.
                For each name in needs, repeat:
                    If (the entry for name in seen) is void, in missing-set, the entry for name becomes true.
                Done.
                If the size of missing-set is greater than 0:
                    Define missing as a series of text.
                    For each pair in missing-set, repeat:
                        Insert the key of pair into missing.
                    Done.
                    The missing becomes cast sorted-ordinally on (missing).
                    Define names as cast quoted-names on (missing, "").
                    Define every-name as a series of text.
                    For each name in missing, repeat:
                        Insert name into every-name.
                    Done.
                    Insert pending's module into every-name.
                    Define all-books as true.
                    For each name in every-name, repeat:
                        If cast one's is-book-name on (name) is false, the all-books becomes false.
                    Done.
                    Define hint as "".
                    If all-books:
                        Define together as a chase.
                        Define first-one as true.
                        For each name in every-name, repeat:
                            If first-one is false, insert ", and " into together.
                            The first-one becomes false.
                            Insert name into together.
                        Done.
                        The hint becomes "Pull them together: 'Pull books on {together converted to text}.'".
                    Done.
                    Otherwise:
                        Define nested as a chase.
                        Define first-one as true.
                        For each name in every-name, repeat:
                            If first-one is false, insert " around " into nested.
                            The first-one becomes false.
                            If cast one's is-book-name on (name), insert "'Pull a book on {name}.'" into nested.
                            Otherwise, insert "'Pull a {name}.'" into nested.
                        Done.
                        The hint becomes "Each is pulled by its own kind, so they nest: {nested converted to text}".
                    Done.
                    Define verb as "aren't".
                    If the number of missing is 1, the verb becomes "isn't".
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{pending's module}' uses {names}, which {verb} pulled here",
                        "A module's dependencies come from the block it is used in, not the one it is written in",
                        pending's line, "pull '{pending's module}' without {names}", hint)).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    Bind node to placed-reference, given (the text name, the number at-row, the number at-column):
        Return cast made on ("VariableReference", a series with (cast quoted on (name), cast numeral on (at-row), cast numeral on (at-column))).
    Done.

    /// `<book>'s member` on a native book — `blueprints'` one member, or none.
    Bind node or failure to infer-book-member unto checker, given (the text book, the text member,
            the number at-row):
        If book is "blueprints" and member is "checksum":
            Define parameters as cast listed.
            Cast parameters's add on (cast plain-type on ("TextType")).
            Define shape as cast plain-type on ("FunctionType").
            Cast shape's add on (parameters).
            Cast shape's add on (cast wrapped on ("VoidableType", cast plain-type on ("BitsType"))).
            Return shape.
        Done.
        Define fix as "Book '{book}' has no members.".
        If book is "blueprints", the fix becomes "Available: 'checksum'.".
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("book '{book}' has no member '{member}'", "",
            at-row, "access '{member}' from book '{book}'", fix)).
    Done.
Done.
